From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hugo Ros <Hugo.Ros@tii.ae>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvgpu: use unlocked dma-buf map helpers on 6.2+

Since Linux 6.2, dma_buf_map_attachment() and dma_buf_unmap_attachment()
require the caller to hold the dma-buf reservation lock. nvgpu_mm_pin()
and nvgpu_mm_unpin() call them without it, which triggers a lockdep warning
for every GPU map/unmap.
Use the _unlocked variants that take the lock.

---
diff --git a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/dmabuf_priv.c b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/dmabuf_priv.c
--- a/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/dmabuf_priv.c
+++ b/nvgpu/drivers/gpu/nvgpu/os/linux/dmabuf_priv.c
@@ -189,7 +189,11 @@
 		return ERR_CAST(attach);
 	}

+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 2, 0)
+	sgt = dma_buf_map_attachment_unlocked(attach, direction);
+#else
 	sgt = dma_buf_map_attachment(attach, direction);
+#endif
 	if (IS_ERR(sgt)) {
 		dma_buf_detach(dmabuf, attach);
 		nvgpu_err(g, "Failed to map attachment (err = %ld)!",
@@ -207,7 +211,11 @@
 			struct dma_buf_attachment *attachment,
 			struct sg_table *sgt)
 {
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 2, 0)
+	dma_buf_unmap_attachment_unlocked(attachment, sgt, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
+#else
 	dma_buf_unmap_attachment(attachment, sgt, DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL);
+#endif
 	dma_buf_detach(dmabuf, attachment);
 }

--
